# Story 6: Named & Detached Sessions (45s)
# Hook: Create a session attached, or spin one up headless as a background daemon.
# Duration: 45s
# Source: story-006-named-detached-sessions.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 5

[00:00.0 --> 00:05.0]
Create a session attached, or spin one up headless as a background daemon.

[00:05.0 --> 00:15.0]
rysh create my-session builds a fresh session and attaches its TUI right away.

[00:15.0 --> 00:27.0]
Add --detached, or just -d, and the daemon spawns headlessly -- no TUI, control returns to your prompt.

[00:27.0 --> 00:36.0]
List your sessions and the headless one is right there, running in the background.

[00:36.0 --> 00:45.0]
Attach to it whenever you like with rysh attach. Detached now, fully interactive when you need it.

